<title>USA: Health Systems Q4 shr loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Health Systems Q4 shr loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>PUEBLO, Colo. 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>			     Q4			    Year</p>
<p>		    1996	 1995	    1996	 1995</p>
<p>Total revenue   802,030    740,961     3,204,156  2,732,052</p>
<p>Depreciation and</p>
<p>   amortization  13,031     12,915	  52,626     48,140</p>
<p>Restructuring and</p>
<p>   other charges 44,108	   --	  44,108	   --</p>
<p>Merger-related</p>
<p>    costs		--	6,724		--     20,164</p>
<p>Total operating</p>
<p>  expenses	816,235    704,977     3,093,109  2,588,904</p>
<p>Operating</p>
<p>    income	(14,205)    35,984	 111,047    143,148</p>
<p>Net interest</p>
<p>    income	  4,786	4,300	  14,163     13,495</p>
<p>Income before income</p>
<p>  taxes	    (9,419)    40,284	 125,210    156,643</p>
<p>Income taxes     (7,179)    17,020	  51,720     67,307</p>
<p>Minority interest in</p>
<p>loss of</p>
<p>    subsidiary	 30	  167	     102	  256</p>
<p>Net income   $   (2,210) $  23,431    $   73,592 $   89,592</p>
<p>Net income per share</p>
<p>- primary and</p>
<p>fully diluted</p>
<p>		 $    (0.05) $    0.48    $     1.52 $     1.83</p>
<p>NOTE: Earnings per share of $2.05 for the full year of 1996, and $.48 per share for the fourth quarter, before the effects of $44 million, or $.53 per share, in restructuring and other charges.</p>
<p>HSI's commercial medical loss ratio (MLR -- medical costs as a percent of premium revenue, excluding ASO revenue) climbed to 81.4 percent in 1996, compared with 79.4 percent in 1995. In 1996's fourth quarter, the MLR for commercial plans was 82.2 percent, compared with 80.2 percent in the final quarter of 1995.</p>
<p>In 1996 the MLR on HSI's Medicare plans was 89.4 percent versus 88.0 percent in 1995.  1996's fourth quarter Medicare MLR was 87.9 percent, against 85.7 percent in the year-earlier period.</p>
